## Derived / referenced work

### LDDC — https://github.com/chenmozhijin/LDDC
License: GPL-3.0-only.

- `app/qrc_crypto.py` contains a Python port of the QRC triple-DES variant
  implementation from LDDC (`LDDC/core/decryptor/tripledes.py`), which itself
  is based on WXRIW/QQMusicDecoder. The port is redistributed under the same
  GPL-3.0 terms.
- API structure concepts for NetEase eapi and QQ Music lyric retrieval were
  informed by LDDC.

### 163MusicLyrics — https://github.com/jitwxs/163MusicLyrics
License: Apache-2.0.

- Product workflow, cookie-login probing, local library scanning and matching
  UX were used as reference. No source files from this project are copied.
- Its API documentation/experience informed the NetEase and QQ Music client
  behavior.

### WXRIW/QQMusicDecoder — https://github.com/WXRIW/QQMusicDecoder
The original C# reference for the non-standard QRC DES implementation.
No source is included directly; the Python implementation descends from the
LDDC port described above.

### qrc-decoder — https://www.npmjs.com/package/qrc-decoder
License: MIT.

- The Tauri/TypeScript rewrite uses the JavaScript implementation of the
  non-standard QRC triple-DES variant for QQ word-level lyric decoding.

